<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">armor</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">armor</ansi> stat measures how much damage you reduce per strike.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

Armor is a maximum percentage of damage absorbed after you try to defend ( blocked, parried, or dodged ).
Each attack is calculated separately for how much it reduces.

Each piece of equipment you wear can add or remove from your Armor total, just as it does other stats.

<ansi fg="cyan">Phase 30g2:</ansi> Shield-bearers can now <ansi fg="command">block</ansi> instead of only reducing damage afterward.
A <ansi fg="command">block</ansi> stops all damage and does not let armor come into play.

